{"page_content": "N\n\nOEC/EC10total (mg Me/kgdw) fOC = fraction organic carbon NOEC/EC10OC, normalised (mg/g OC)\n\nThe PNEC sediment can be translated back to mg/kg dry wt. when a default OC value is assumed for the area/region under investigation. In the EU, a standard sediment has a default OC value of 5 % (example 3-3). In a similar way, the normalization could be performed with other sediment ligands such as Fe/Mn oxy hydroxides when it can be shown that a relationship exists between the observed toxicity and the ligand.\n\nE\n\nxample 3-3: organic carbon normalization (Cu)\n\nThe effect of organic carbon on the toxicity of copper was observed for all sediment species but explicitly proven by conducting tests with OECD sediments (containing no AVS) with high (9.8 % OC) and low (2.6% OC) organic carbon concentrations for the species Tubifex, Hyalella and Chironomus (Table 10).\n\nTable 10: Means and ranges (across endpoints) of the ratio NOEC or EC50 in 9.8% OC to the NOEC or EC50 in 2.6% OC", "metadata": {"doc_id": "136fc29d-a4d9-4585-997b-1cd9f25255e5", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "information_requirements_r7_13_2_en.pdf"}}